0,Creole music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creole_music,"Creole folk songs originated on the plantations of the French and Spanish colonists of Louisiana. The music characteristics embody African-derived syncopated rhythms, the habanera accent of Spain, and the quadrille of France.",Réunion French Creole,Creole
1,Haitian Creole - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haitian_Creole,"Haitian Creole (Haitian Creole: kreyòl ayisyen, [kɣejɔl ajisjɛ]), or simply Creole (kreyòl), is a French-based creole language with a Romance foundation and significant Atlantic-Congo structural influences.",Réunion French Creole,Creole
